        <div id="who" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            10. Who Should Buy Body Fortress, and Who Should Skip It
          </h2>

          <p>
            <strong>Buy it</strong> if your main goal is cheap protein from a brand you can find in almost any Walmart, pharmacy or supermarket, you tolerate regular whey, and you do not mind sucralose. In that case, the 3.9 lb chocolate or vanilla tub at a big-box price is one of the best deals in the aisle, and the 30 g scoop makes hitting a daily protein target easy. It also suits people who want a heavier, more filling shake and are not counting every calorie.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Skip it</strong> if you compete in a drug-tested sport, because we could not find a sport-level certification. Skip it if you avoid artificial sweeteners, if regular whey concentrate gives you bloating, or if you are cutting hard and want the leanest possible scoop. Skip it on Amazon whenever the price per 25 g comes in above about $1.50, because better powders cost less there. And if you already take a multivitamin with zinc, think twice about drinking two scoops a day.
          </p>

          <p>
            For lactose-sensitive buyers, the <strong>Super Advanced Isolate</strong> is a better fit than the whey, but read the label: its isolate blend includes milk protein isolate, which contains casein, alongside hydrolyzed whey isolate and whey isolate. That is fine for most people and makes the shake slightly thicker and slower digesting, but it is not a pure whey isolate and it is still a dairy product. True milk allergy means no Body Fortress product is safe. Our <a href="/best-lactose-free-protein-powder/">best lactose-free protein powder</a> guide has options.
          </p>

          <p>
            How to use it well: one scoop in 10 to 12 ounces of milk or water after training or with a light breakfast is the simplest routine. Use the two-scoop serving only if you genuinely need 60 g in one sitting, which most people do not. Count the vitamins if you take other supplements. Compare cost per 25 g every time you restock, because Body Fortress pricing swings more between retailers than almost any brand we track. For the full ranking of store-shelf powders, our <a href="/best-walmart-protein-powder/">best Walmart protein powder</a> guide is the next stop.
          </p>
        </div>

